<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/070V">Example <span data-tag="070V">9.7.4.5</span>.</a> Let $\mathbb {K}$ be the collection of all finite simplicial sets. Then $\operatorname{\mathcal{S}}_{&lt; \mathbb {K} }$ can be identified with the full subcategory $\operatorname{\mathcal{S}}_{ \mathrm{fin} } \subset \operatorname{\mathcal{S}}$ spanned by the essentially finite Kan complexes (see Definition <a data-tag="067P" href="/tag/067P">9.2.6.1</a>). This is a reformulation of Proposition <a data-tag="067R" href="/tag/067R">9.2.6.3</a>. </p>
